# build output (regenerate with tools/site/build.py). Anchored to the repo root: an unanchored
# "site/" also matched tools/site/ and kept the whole generator out of git.
/site/*
# ...except the images the pages actually show, so a Netlify build from git publishes them (2026-11-09). All are
# Wikimedia Commons files (public domain, CC0, CC BY or CC BY-SA; credits and licenses in
# data/editions/<ed>/images.csv). Only the 320x400 thumbnails the people page uses are tracked, plus Hiler's
# portrait, which is already small and has no thumbnail. The large originals stay local. A new photo needs its
# thumb_<image_id>.jpg here, or the build's --check fails on the missing file (that is the safety net).
!/site/images/
/site/images/*
!/site/images/thumb_*.jpg
!/site/images/Congressman_John_P._Hiler.png

# browser-test logs
.playwright-mcp/

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# binary source downloads (~1.6 GB); URLs are recorded in data/**/sources_*.csv
sources/**/*.pdf
sources/**/*.PDF
sources/**/*.zip
sources/**/*.jpg
sources/**/*.jpeg
sources/**/*.png
sources/**/*.xlsx
sources/**/*.docx

# scratch
research/tmp/
*.bak
*.bak-*

# raw full-text dumps of source documents (may contain private individuals' contact details; regenerate from the PDFs)
sources/recovered/**/*.txt
!sources/recovered/laville-rename/notes.txt
